pve-ups-panel (2.2.9) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add pve-ups-shutdown: new executor script that actually enforces the
    VM/CT shutdown rules configured in the Shutdown panel.
    - monitor <ups_target>: forks a background daemon that polls upsc
      every 30 seconds; shuts down VMs/CTs whose per-rule charge/runtime
      thresholds are crossed (in priority order); when global thresholds
      are crossed the node itself is shut down via /sbin/shutdown.
    - recover <ups_target>: stops the monitor, waits for battery charge
      to reach charge_before_start, then restarts VMs/CTs in reverse
      priority order (only those with action=shutdown; force-stopped
      guests are left alone).
    - cancel: stops the monitor and clears all state files.
    - State tracked in /var/run/pve-ups-panel/: shutdown-monitor.pid,
      shutdown-done, guests-shut. Config reloaded on every poll cycle
      so live changes take effect without restart.
  * pve-ups-notify: call pve-ups-shutdown monitor on ONBATT/LOWBATT
    events and pve-ups-shutdown recover on ONLINE events (non-blocking
    fork so upsmon is not held up).
  * debian/postinst: create /var/run/pve-ups-panel/ and set +x on
    pve-ups-shutdown.
  * debian/pve-ups-panel.install: add pve-ups-shutdown to package.

 -- YoMin Su <aaaa1234567891016@gmail.com>  Sun, 31 May 2026 18:00:00 +0800

pve-ups-panel (2.2.8) stable; urgency=medium

  * Config.pm: fix NOTIFYFLAG lost on any device/server config change.
    _build_upsmon_conf previously read NOTIFYFLAG from the existing
    upsmon.conf (written by Notify.pm). If a device operation happened
    before notification rules were first saved, there was nothing to
    preserve, and any subsequent Config.pm rewrite would silently drop
    NOTIFYFLAG. Fix: _build_upsmon_conf now reads notify-rules.json
    directly (same source Notify.pm uses) to regenerate NOTIFYFLAG on
    every rewrite. notify-rules.json is the single source of truth;
    upsmon.conf is always consistent with it regardless of operation
    order. Add use JSON and NUT_NOTIFY_EVENTS constant to Config.pm.

