pve-ups-panel (2.2.7) stable; urgency=medium

  * Architecture: device names are now plain names throughout the UI.
    The backend resolves a plain name to its upsc target internally, so
    the frontend never needs to know about name@host:port details.
  * UPS.pm: replace _list_configured_devices() with _device_target_map()
    (returns { name => upsc_target } hash). GET /ups now accepts a plain
    device name, resolves to the correct upsc target (local: name, remote:
    name@host[:port]), and returns plain names in _ups_name and _available.
    RRD files are keyed by plain name, not the stripped upsc target.
  * UPS/Battery.pm: add _resolve_upsc_target() helper (reads ups.conf and
    upsmon.conf). GET and POST /battery now sanitise the ups param to a
    plain name then resolve before passing to upsc / upscmd.
  * pve-ups-panel.js: revert v2.2.6 name@host reconstruction in
    _loadDevices. DeviceSelector consistently shows and sends plain device
    names; all three tabs (Overview, History, Battery Health) stay in sync.

