pve-ups-panel (2.2.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Config.pm: separate local and remote NUT accounts. upsmon_local
    replaces the old hardcoded upsmon/localmonitor account. upsmon_local
    carries upsmon master + instcmds = ALL + actions = SET, giving the
    local monitoring process full command authority (battery tests, etc.)
    without exposing admin credentials over the network. A separate
    configurable slave account is written to upsd.users only when a
    remote_user + remote_password are set via the new server endpoint.
  * Config.pm: manage upsd.conf. _generate_upsd_conf() / _read_upsd_conf()
    added. set_mode now writes upsd.conf automatically: standalone forces
    LISTEN 127.0.0.1, netserver opens to 0.0.0.0 (unless a custom address
    was already set). _fix_nut_perms now also chmods upsd.conf.
  * Config.pm: add GET /ups/config/server → {listen_addr, remote_user,
    has_remote_password}. Add PUT /ups/config/server → updates upsd.conf
    listen address, rewrites upsd.users with separated accounts, and
    normalises any localhost MONITOR entries in upsmon.conf to upsmon_local.
    Password is preserved if remote_password parameter is omitted.
  * Config.pm: add_device (usb/snmp) now uses upsmon_local for the
    localhost MONITOR line. Existing localhost monitors are migrated to
    upsmon_local on each write (upgrade compatibility). delete_device
    normalises remaining monitors likewise.
  * Config.pm: _get_or_create_local_password() reads the existing
    upsmon_local password from upsd.users on each call, generating a
    32-char random password only on first use.
  * pve-ups-panel.js: add PVE.ups.ServerSettingsWindow. Loads current
    listen_addr and remote_user via GET /ups/config/server; saves via
    PUT. Password fields are optional (blank = keep existing). Confirm
    Password field validates match client-side.
  * pve-ups-panel.js: DevicePanel mode bar gains a right-aligned
    "Server Settings" button (gear icon) that appears only when mode is
    netserver and opens ServerSettingsWindow.
  * i18n: add 11 strings for server settings in 31 languages.

